*.bak
# Lane-created pre-edit backups (e.g. tools/oc-x.pre-20260925-115731). Generated
# residue: they accumulate, nothing reaps them, and because oc-ledger's
# stray-guard reads a full `git status --porcelain`, a single UNTRACKED one
# blocks every version bump with die 7. Same class as *.bak above.
*.pre-*

# The battery red-receipt transcript (#517/#614). Since #614 the receipt embeds
# its own evidence (fail_rows), so this file is a transient human-readable
# transcript, not a durable artifact -- and being untracked it tripped the
# sync stray-guard (die 7) while a red was under investigation.
tools/tests/battery-last-fail.log

# Runtime review artefacts (Duty-4 proposals, Duty-6 reports, evidence).
# These belong to the STATE repo (opencrabs-dev/reviews/), which is where the
# intake lane reads and where oc-ledger's TRACKED sweep covers them. Lanes that
# write them into the SKILL repo instead create an untracked path -- and because
# the sync stray-guard reads a full `git status --porcelain`, ONE lane's misplaced
# proposal directory blocks every version bump with die 7. Live instance
# 2026-09-27: reviews/20260927-c25/ held 7 files, 6 of them duplicates of state-repo
# copies and ONE (telegram-95bec69b-1.md) with no counterpart anywhere -- so both
# "delete" and "rehome" would have destroyed a real submission. Ignoring the class
# is non-destructive: the stray file stays on disk and on someone's record.
reviews/
